You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Context Label Cursor (`cursor-context-label`)

A cursor that reads the room: over elements marked data-cursor="View" (or Drag, Play…) the dot morphs into a pill showing that label in the element's colour; elsewhere it's a small difference-blend dot.

## What it should do
Build a contextual cursor: inside a container hide the native cursor, track the pointer into springy motion values, find the closest [data-cursor] ancestor of the event target and morph a dot (12 px, mix-blend-difference) into a pill sized to the label with data-cursor-color as background; crossfade labels.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **motion**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/cursor-context-label.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** Native cursor is hidden only on fine pointers inside the area; every target is still a real link/button with its own name. Off on touch.
- **Performance:** Spring motion values; label swaps only when the hovered target changes.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

